+    <key name="xwayland-scaling-mode"
+         enum="org.gnome.mutter.MetaXwaylandScalingMode">
+      <default>'automatic'</default>
+      <summary>Configure how the Xwayland coordinate space is scaled</summary>
+      <description>
+        Controls how the Xwayland coordinate space (and thus the root window
+        size visible to X11 clients) is derived from the monitor configuration.
+
+        “automatic” scales the Xwayland coordinate space by the ceiling of the
+        highest monitor scale. On a monitor using a fractional scale this means
+        Xwayland renders at a higher resolution than the monitor and the result
+        is downscaled by the compositor.
+
+        “native” makes the Xwayland coordinate space match the physical
+        resolution of the monitor. X11 content is then presented 1:1 and is not
+        rendered at a higher resolution than necessary, at the cost of X11 user
+        interfaces appearing smaller on fractional scales. This only has an
+        effect in the logical monitor layout mode; the physical layout mode
+        always behaves this way.
+
+        This key is overridden when the “xwayland-scaling-factor” key is set to
+        a non-zero value.
+      </description>
+    </key>
+
